### Section 3: Final Post-Incident Report

# Post-Incident & Remediation Report: `ledger-prod-us-east`

## 1. Incident Root Cause Analysis

On October 24, 2023, cluster `ledger-prod-us-east` experienced a degradation in P99 write latency ($68.5\text{ms}$ vs SLA target $L_{\max} \le 45\text{ms}$). Diagnostics revealed that **Node 3** (`node-03.us-east.internal`) suffered a localized disk I/O degradation (`disk_iops_util` = $94.8\%$, queue depth = 128) following a transient network partition.

The disk I/O bottleneck caused disk `fsync` operations on Node 3 to block, resulting in a WAL replication lag of $\Delta_{commit, 3} = 2,080$ log entries (violating the threshold of 1,500 entries) and physical corruptions in un-flushed WAL tail blocks (`00000000000005a2.wal`). The leader (`node-01.us-east.internal`) was forced to continuously retry log replication to Node 3, causing replication queue bloat and degraded P99 write latencies across the entire cluster.

